The system is a Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) platform supporting multi-user operations with role hierarchy, temporary delegation, clearance-based authorization, and concurrent request processing. The system enforces security constraints such as clearance-based permissions, role delegation and revocation, and preserves safety, liveness, and integrity under concurrent operations. A new Emergency Module is to be integrated, enabling special operational modes and privileges during emergencies, with specific triggering, duration, and exit requirements.

EXISTING-SYSTEM ASSUMPTIONS AND CONSTRAINTS
===========================================
- Users possess security clearance levels: High, Medium, or Low.
- Administrators have High clearance, but not all High-clearance users are Administrators.
- Roles can be assigned or delegated, subject to clearance and minimum-role clearance requirements.
